initial commit:

This version upon start runs continuous background sync that fetches all 19 genres x 500 pages from TMDB
clicking on the moviecard or a torrent ijn the list starts a download, movie automatically plays when there is data buffered

known issue:

the when clicking on the next/prev page buttons the total pages count changes and its slow
I think the search is being run every time

fixed - pagination now uses in-memory data:

- Added /api/popular/all endpoint to return full movie list from cache
- Frontend now loads all popular movies once on startup
- Next/Prev buttons now slice from in-memory array instead of calling API
- Page count is calculated from array length, no longer fluctuates
- Search results also stored in-memory for pagination
- Initial search still shows live progress, but navigation after is instant

changes:

- reorganized cache storage:
  - Created database/ directory for movie cache
  - Renamed movies_cache.json to database/active.json
  - Updated CACHE_FILE path in movietime

- added dark scrollbars to match the theme

- removed 24 hour cache expiry, cache now never expires

- added continuous background movie sync:
  - On app start, background thread continuously fetches TMDB pages one at a time
  - New movies are added incrementally to avoid duplicates (O(1) lookup via set)
  - Saves sync state (current_page) to database/sync_state.json for resume on restart
  - After page 500, loops back to page 1
  - Rate limited to 25 req/sec (0.04 sec between requests)
  - Uses atomic file writes (write to temp, then rename) for safe shutdown
  - Graceful shutdown: sets stop event on exit, waits up to 3 seconds for thread to finish
  - Added /api/sync/status endpoint to monitor sync progress
  - Removed initial bulk fetch - now handled by continuous background sync
  - Updated /api/cache/refresh to indicate continuous sync is running
  - Writes to disk every 100 pages to reduce I/O overhead

- replaced single-file approach with dual-file append-only system:
  - active.json: main movie database (line-delimited JSON)
  - building.json: append-only file for new movies (line-delimited JSON)
  - On each page: append new movies to building.json, validate, then atomic swap
  - After swap: building contains old active data + new movies (both in sync)
  - Only writes ~20 new movies per page instead of rewriting entire dataset
  - O(1) I/O regardless of total database size
  - Added recovery: if one file corrupted, copy from the other
  - Both files now use consistent line-delimited format
  - Added ensure_database_files() to handle first-run edge cases
  - Fixed validation to properly parse line-delimited JSON
  - Fixed load_cached_movies() to use line-delimited format parser

- added genre-based discovery:
  - Uses /discover/movie with with_genres parameter to fetch by genre
  - 19 genre IDs defined (Action, Adventure, Animation, Comedy, etc.)
  - Two-phase sync: Phase 1 = popular (500 pages), Phase 2 = interleaved genre search
  - Interleaved: For each page 1-500, cycles through all 19 genres
  - Sync state now tracks current_page, genre_index, and phase
  - Saves state after each page for resume capability
  - Reuses Update Movies button as manual refresh to reload movie list from database
  - Renamed /api/popular/all to /api/movies/all to reflect it now returns all movies (popular + genre)

- replaced Update button with automatic movie count display:
   - Removed Update Movies button entirely
   - Added movie count display (e.g., "4,523 Movies") in pagination area
   - Auto-refresh polls every 10 seconds to check for new movies
   - Count updates automatically without user interaction
   - Layout: sort | n Movies | prev | page n of n | next

- added genre-based filtering:
   - Replaced Type dropdown with Genre dropdown (19 genres)
   - Frontend filters movies by genre_ids field
   - Backend now includes genre_ids in movie data

- added "N of T Movies" display:
   - Shows filtered count (N) of total cache count (T)
   - When search or genre filter active, displays "N of T Movies"
   - When no filter, displays just "T Movies"

- fixed auto-refresh movie count bug:
   - Auto-refresh now updates total count and pages when no filter active
   - When user is viewing all movies, count and pages update every 10 seconds
   - When filter is active, display stays unchanged until new search

- changed download directory:
   - Changed from ./downloads to ./download

- fixed search pagination with genre filter:
   - Search progress poll now applies genre filter to results
   - Previously used unfiltered results causing wrong page count

- fixed search with genre filter returning no results:
   - Search results now include genre_ids field
   - Backend search now includes genre_ids from TMDB
   - Previously missing genre_ids caused genre filter to find 0 results

- fixed apibay results filtered out by genre:
   - Genre filter now shows results without genre_ids (apibay results)
   - Changed filter to: !m.genre_ids || m.genre_ids.includes(genreId)
   - Previously: m.genre_ids && m.genre_ids.includes(genreId) removed all non-TMDB results

- removed focus outlines:
   - Removed orange outline on dropdowns and inputs
   - Removed input focus box-shadow
   - Added global outline: none

- made movie description text bold:
   - Description overlay text is now bold
   - Made all text bold globally (dropdowns, buttons, links, etc)

- fixed torrent hover not fetching:
   - Added missing currentCategory variable
   - Was undefined, breaking torrent API calls

- added header-ready playback check:
   - New /api/download/playable endpoint
   - Checks minimum 5MB downloaded AND header pieces ready
   - Also waits for metadata to arrive (start_piece must be set)
   - Prevents playback starting before video header is downloaded
   - Fixed glitchy playback from starting at random position

- added debug logging:
   - Backend /api/play logs video_file, valid, file_size, errors
   - Backend /api/download/playable logs all check values
   - Debug log stored in debug.log file
   - Frontend sends debug to backend /api/debug

- added rating filter:
   - Replaced sort dropdown with rating dropdown
   - Options: All, 1+ through 9+
   - Filters results by minimum rating

- fixed rating filter display reset on auto-refresh:
   - Auto-refresh now preserves "N of T Movies" format when rating filter active
   - Previously only checked genre and search filters, ignoring rating

- reversed rating menu order:
   - Now shows All at top, then 9+ down to 1+ (highest first)
   - Removed redundant 0+ option (same as All)

- added "None" option to rating filter:
   - Shows only movies without a rating
   - Handles rating values of null, "None", 0, or empty string in database

- fixed rating filter only filtering current page:
   - handleRatingChange() now filters from full displayMovies array
   - Previously filtered from currentMovies (just page 1's 100 movies)
   - Fixed pagination and display to work correctly with filter

- expanded header and movie grid to full window width:
   - Removed max-width: 1200px constraint from header
   - Movie grid now uses full window width
   - Cards automatically adjust to fit more per row based on screen size

- swapped rating and genre dropdown positions:
   - Rating dropdown now appears before Genre dropdown
   - Maintains same filter functionality

- added year filter dropdown:
   - New dropdown between Rating and Genre
   - Options: All, then 2026 down to 1901
   - Filters movies by exact release year
   - Integrated into filter system and auto-refresh

- fixed dropdown scrollbar colors:
   - Added custom scrollbar styling to select elements
   - Uses same #0099ff color scheme as page scrollbars

- added incremental sync for movie updates:
   - Backend now tracks movie_count in memory
   - Backend compares current count vs last_movie_count from sync_state.json
   - On poll: if count increased, returns only new movies (incremental: true)
   - If count decreased, returns full list (full sync needed)
   - If count same, returns empty movies array (no change)
   - Frontend 10s interval now appends vs replaces based on incremental flag
   - Significantly reduces bandwidth when no new movies
   - Zero file reads when count unchanged

================================================================================
Session 2 - Async rewrite and new_movies optimization:

- simplified background sync to cycle through 19 genres continuously:
  - Uses async parallel fetching (40 concurrent requests)
  - Fetches all 500 pages per genre in parallel (~3 seconds per genre)
  - No page tracking needed - always starts at page 1
  - Saves only current_genre_index to sync_state.json for resume
  - Removed popular/fetch_and_cache_popular_movies() initial load
  - Removed phase and current_page tracking

- renamed database files:
  - active.json → movies_active.json
  - building.json → movies_building.json

- added ensure_new_movies_files() function for new_movies file protection

- optimized background sync with new_movies double-buffer:
  - New database/new_movies_active.json and new_movies_building.json (atomic swap)
  - Sync writes to new_movies_building (not main database)
  - Ensure files exist on swap with ensure_new_movies_files()
  - Swap in API: new_movies_active ← new_movies_building
  - Then update main database via building swap (active ← building)
  - API sends new movies, then updates main database
  - Clear new_movies_building after each poll
  - Initial load (?full=1) reads active.json for full history
  - Fixed: poll returns main database total (not new_movies buffer total)

- removed qwebchannel:
  - Removed serve_qwebchannel route and pywebchannel.js lookup
  - Removed PyQtBridge class and QWebChannel setup
  - Was set up but never used by frontend
  - Folder button uses Flask API, not pyqt bridge

- Fixed validation treats empty files as valid:
  - validate_json_file() now returns True for empty files instead of False
  - Previously empty files were treated as corrupted

- Fixed new_movies accumulation flow:
  - Sync no longer clears during genre changes
  - All 19 genres accumulate unique movies in new_movies_building continuously
  - Sync keeps looping, movies keep accumulating
  - Poll reads when requested: sends to UI, main db updates, then clears
  - Only cleared AFTER new movies sent to frontend
  - Ready for next batch

- Fixed sync runs continuously:
  - Added check to prevent sync from stopping after one genre cycle
  - Sync now loops through all 19 genres indefinitely

- Changed poll interval from 10 seconds to 1 second:
   - UI polls for new movies every 1 second for faster updates

- Added debug logging to background sync:
   - Added [SYNC] prefix to all sync-related prints for easier debugging
   - Added try/except around entire while loop to catch silent exceptions
   - Added traceback print on exception to identify root cause
   - Added print at start of while loop to verify re-entry on second cycle
   - Helps diagnose why sync stops after second cycle

- Fixed sync loop printing "Background sync stopped" after every cycle:
   - The status=stopped and print lines were inside the while loop
   - Moved them outside the while loop so they only run on actual app shutdown
   - Loop now runs forever correctly

- Fixed auto-refresh not updating movie count:
   - Changed poll interval from 10000ms (10s) back to 1000ms (1s)
   - Total now updates every poll regardless of whether new movies are returned
   - Previously total only updated when movies array was non-empty
   - Count now updates in real-time as sync adds movies to database

- Fixed race condition causing sync to stop early:
   - Added new_movies_lock to protect new_movies file operations
   - Sync thread now acquires lock when writing to new_movies_building.json
   - Poll API acquires lock when validating, swapping, and clearing new_movies files
   - Prevents validation errors from corrupt reads during concurrent writes

- Fixed movie cards not updating when new movies arrive:
   - Added renderMovies() call after updating displayMovies in poll response
   - Recalculates currentMovies from updated displayMovies (respects current page)
   - New movies now appear in grid without needing restart or search
   - Changed poll interval to 5 seconds for less frequent updates

- Simplified poll logic:
   - Poll now transfers ALL movies from buffer to main DB each time
   - No tracking of previous counts - each poll processes current buffer
   - Clear new_movies_building after transfer so sync can add more
   - Much simpler logic that matches the requested design

- Renamed loadPopular to loadAll:
   - Function was loading all movies from database, not just popular
   - Updated function name and related comments for clarity

================================================================================
Session 3 - Search optimization and bug fixes:

- Moved TMDB_API_KEY from hardcoded to .tmdb file:
   - Created .tmdb file with raw API key
   - Removed hardcoded key from source
   - Added .tmdb to .gitignore
   - Implemented load_env_file() function to read key

- Fixed pagination with dropdown filters:
   - changePage() now applies current genre/rating/year filters
   - Previously used unfiltered displayMovies causing wrong results

- Fixed search results overwritten by auto-refresh:
   - Auto-refresh now skips when currentSource === 'search'
   - Previously replaced search results with popular movies

- Made search default to local-only:
   - Added local=1 parameter to search API
   - Search now uses only local cache + apibay (no TMDb API)
   - Auto-refresh re-runs local search to update results
   - Much faster than hitting TMDb on every poll

- Made auto-refresh only update UI when data changes:
   - Added lastTotalMovies tracking
   - Non-search mode: only updates if totalDatabaseMovies changes
   - Search mode: only updates if search result count changes
   - Prevents flickering/reset of movie cards during hover

- Fixed movie count showing "N of N" instead of "N of T":
   - Added totalDatabaseMovies variable from backend
   - Backend returns total_database in search response
   - All movie count displays now use totalDatabaseMovies
   - Shows correct "247 of 119000 Movies" format

- Fixed background sync not fetching movies:
   - load_env_file() was defined after TMDB_API_KEY was set to None
   - Moved function definition before it's called
   - Sync now correctly reads key from .tmdb file

- Removed debug print statements:
   - Removed TMDB_API_KEY debug print
   - Removed per-page fetch debug prints